This code solves the Best Time to Buy and Sell Stock (single transaction) problem.

It iterates through the prices array once.
Keeps track of the minimum price seen so far (minPrice).
For each price:

If it's lower than minPrice, update minPrice (best day to buy).
Otherwise, calculate profit (price - minPrice) and update maxProfit if it's higher.

In short:
Buy at the lowest price so far and sell at the current price if it gives better profit.

Complexity Analysis
Time Complexity: O(n)
→ Only one pass through the array.

Space Complexity: O(1)
→ Uses only a few variables (no extra data structures).
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
class Solution {
    public int maxProfit(int[] prices) {
       int minPrice=Integer.MAX_VALUE;
       int maxProfit=0;
       for(int price: prices){
        if(price<minPrice){
        minPrice=price;
       }else{
        int profit= price-minPrice;
        maxProfit= Math.max(maxProfit,profit);
       }
      
    }
     return maxProfit;
    
}
}
